  "main_text": "Live Better, Earn Rewards\nJoin for free and Get points with every purchase—making your space better should pay off.\nJoin Now\nSign In\nWAYS TO REDEEM\nRedeem your rewards for various offers (gifts, products & coupons) with Garvee points\nLog in to enjoy double savings: use your points and most coupons together!\nREDEEMING IS EASY\nOnly 3 Steps-Turn your points into discounts!\nSign Up / Log In To Unlock Your Welcome Bonus:\nGet 10%+$20 OFF & 100 Points\nSign Up / Log In\nWAYS TO EARN\nEarn points by completing these actions\nVIP TIERS\nSign up or log in to see your current loyalty level and corresponding benefits.\nSign up / log in\nBronze\nSign up to join\n1x points on spending\n($1 = 1 pts)\nNew member: 10%+$20 coupon\nBirthday reward: 50 points\nSilver\nRequire 400 pts\n2x points on spending\n($1 = 2 pts)\n5% OFF on selected items\nBirthday reward: $5 coupon\nGold\nRequire 1200 pts\n3x points on spending\n($1 = 3 pts)\n8% OFF on more items\nDedicated support\nBirthday reward: $10 coupon\nDiamond\nRequire 2400 pts\n5x points on spending\n($1 = 5 pts)\n10% OFF on almost all items\n72-hour VIP early access to sales\nUnlock Any Product for $1 in Exclusive Section\nBirthday reward: $20 coupon + exclusive gift\nFREQUENT ASKED QUESTIONS\n1.How do I join the loyalty program?\nSimply sign up to create your account and start earning rewards!\n2.How do I earn GARVEE Points?\nEarn points by signing up, making purchases, and more! Check out the “Ways to Earn” section for details.\n3.How do I use GARVEE Points?\nLog in, visit your dashboard, and select the “Ways to Redeem” section to redeem your points for rewards.\n4.Where can I see my points balance?\nFirst, log in to your account! Your points balance will be highlighted in a box on the top of the page.\n5.How long are my points valid?\nThe validity period of points is 1 year, calculated from the date of point acquisition. The points will expire in a rolling manner. For example, if the point validity date is January 1st, 2025, the validity period will end on January 1st, 2026."
}